  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 308 AM EDT Tue Sep 8 2026\n\n- Showers/storms tonight/Wednesday\n\nA cold front stretches from eastern North Dakota to central South\nDakota. Radar and IR imagery shows abundant convection firing\nahead of the front currently. As the front approaches Michigan\ntonight, we're likely to see showers and thunderstorms move over\nthe far northwest cwa late this afternoon and slowly move south\nacross the cwa tonight and Wednesday. All of the ECMWF ensemble\nmembers show precipitation. Upper level flow is largely parallel \nto the front so we're not going to see the front plow through \nquickly.\n\nA nocturnal LLJ will move over the cwa tonight advecting in\nmoisture-rich air from the south; pwats climb to around 2 inches,\nwhich could result in moderate to locally heavy rainfall. However, \nMUCAPE is only a couple hundred j/kg. Thus thunderstorms may not\nbe very robust and severe storms are not anticipated. RRFS model \ndata has back off on thunderstorm strength during the past couple \nof model runs. That said, bulk shear values are in the 30-40kt \nrange tonight and a bit higher Wednesday which may allow for\nlocally stronger cells. Total qpf expected is a quarter inch or\nless south of I-96 and a quarter to two thirds north of I-96. \n\nPrecipitation will diminish Wednesday afternoon as the front moves\nsouth and high pressure begins to move in from the northwest. \n\n- Low chance of showers Saturday\n\nAnother front will approach Saturday, but the strongest dynamics\nwith the system will be north in Canada, closer to the low over\nJames Bay. Moisture return ahead of the front also isn't stellar,\nso we only have 15-20 PoPs in the grids for this.\n\n- Stronger system possible Monday\n\nA better chance of rain will arrive next Monday when another front\napproaches. This time, though, there's a much stronger shortwave\naccompanying it. Models show a tighter pressure gradient which\ncould mean a breezy day ahead of the system. Most of the ECMWF\nensemble members show precipitation with this system, and a few\npoint toward heavy rain; there's time to flesh out the details as\nit is almost a week away.",
